  "personNames": {
    "source": "plan/kararlar/ADR-041-m5-part1-sonu-cevaplari.md",
    "why": "ADR-041 #72 (K-523): a professional app names no person — not the coach whose experience the rules rest on, not the people who built it. The app, the API contract and the product's code say what kind of source a rule has; the research path (arastirma/…, internal, read on the server for audit) is taken out before the scan, so a path may hold a name. Case is spelled out in the pattern (no case-insensitive flag, the same in Java and JavaScript): a name is not glued to a lowercase letter on either side, but a capital starts a word, so code names are caught — GURAY_LOSS_CAP, gurayLossCap, fromLevent — and 'eleventh' or 'Leventis' are not.",
    "pattern": "(?:(?<![a-z])|(?=[GL]))([gG]([uU]|ü|Ü)[rR][aA][yY]|[lL][eE][vV][eE][nN][tT])(?![a-z])",
